      m_Calls: []
  m_text: '                           Metal Sewer Pipes

    -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

    Common
    types: Cast iron, steel, precast reinforced concrete.



    Advantages:



    High
    strength & durability: Cast iron can withstand very high pressure (up to ~4800
    psi).



    Structural stability: Rigid and stable, ideal for heavy loads and
    deep.



    Fire resistance: Concrete and steel resist fire and extreme temperatures.



    Long
    history & proven performance: Used in large municipal systems for decades.

    Disadvantages:



    Corrosion
    risk: Cast iron and steel can rust over time, leading to leaks and structural
    weakness



    Root intrusion: Older cast iron lines are vulnerable to root
    penetration



    Heavy & costly: More labor-intensive and expensive to install



    Maintenance
    needs: Requires protective coatings or regular inspection to prevent corrosion '
